==Battleground==
*2 [[Master A.|Master As]] spawn, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*3 [[Master A.|Master As]] spawn after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 24 seconds<sup>720f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 25.33 seconds<sup>760f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 2~10 seconds<sup>60f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
You will need heavy attackers, such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]], and any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] to deal with the Owlbrows, it is highly recommended you use [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed M. Titan Cat]] to hurt the Master As. However, the Master As also spawn continuously, so the Titan Cats will be unable to hurt the Master As meaning long-ranged attackers, like [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]], are mandatory.

This stage can also easily be beaten by waiting for the Owlbrows, getting past the Master A., and killing them with something like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]], [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]]. Then just spam ([[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed]]) [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cats]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]], [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]], [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]], [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat]] and everything else that can damage the Master As. The Owlbrows should keep your money up.

